-- INSTALL for Hackedbox - an X Window Manager (C) 2026 --

## Compilation and Installation:

Hackedbox uses the GNU Autotools build system.

Before compiling from a source checkout, generate the build system with:

./bootstrap

Configure Hackedbox with:

./configure --prefix=/usr

The `--prefix=/usr` option installs Hackedbox into the standard system
directories.

Compile Hackedbox with:

make -j$(nproc)

Install Hackedbox with:

sudo make install

The complete build sequence is:

./bootstrap
./configure --prefix=/usr
make -j$(nproc)
sudo make install

## Configuration:

Run:

./configure --help

to display the available configuration and build options.

The most commonly used option is:

--prefix=DIR

Set the installation prefix.

For example:

./configure --prefix=/usr

## Build Cleanup:

To remove compiled object files and binaries from the source tree:

make clean

To remove generated configuration files and return the source tree to
an unconfigured state:

make distclean

If the Autotools files need to be regenerated from the source tree:

./bootstrap

## Dependencies:

Hackedbox requires X11 development libraries and the libraries required
by its current image, font, and rendering systems.

See the `DEPENDENCIES` file for the current list of required libraries,
development headers, and build tools.

The dependency list is maintained separately from this file so it can
be updated as the Hackedbox source tree changes.

## Installation Layout:

When configured with:

./configure --prefix=/usr

Hackedbox installs its executables under:

/usr/bin/

Hackedbox data files are installed under:

/usr/share/hackedbox/

This includes:

/usr/share/hackedbox/styles/
/usr/share/hackedbox/backgrounds/
/usr/share/hackedbox/menu

## Documentation:

Additional documentation is available throughout the source tree.

README
    General project information.

DEPENDENCIES
    Build dependencies and required libraries.

data/README
    Information about installed Hackedbox data files.

data/README.menu
    Menu configuration and syntax.

data/README.style
    Style configuration and available resources.

doc/README.setup
    Hackedbox setup and configuration information.

doc/README.hbsetbg
    Documentation for the hbsetbg background utility.

doc/
    Additional Hackedbox documentation and manual pages.

## HbTK:

HbTK is developed as an independent toolkit and is no longer built as
part of the Hackedbox window manager.

The HbTK project has its own source tree and build system.

See the HbTK documentation for its separate compilation and installation
instructions.

## Development:

Hackedbox is currently developed and tested on:

Linux x86_64
Xorg
X11

Hackedbox is designed around the X11 protocol and does not require a
desktop environment.

The project does not depend on GTK, Qt, or a desktop environment for
the window manager itself.

## Reporting Build Problems:

When reporting a build problem, include:

- Hackedbox version
- operating system
- architecture
- compiler version
- configure command
- relevant error messages
- relevant build output

This information makes build problems easier to reproduce and diagnose.

